{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MyYESY8QhpvEF686LhvVHQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu OAuth API scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR:WRITE authorize token refresh_token expires_in\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\"},{\"title\":\"Überauth intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090.md\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\"},{\"title\":\"open api\",\"url\":\"https://www.intervals.icu/features/open-api/\"},{\"title\":\"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io\",\"url\":\"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/latest/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"intervals icu tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\"},{\"title\":\"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io\",\"url\":\"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/docs/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=9\"}]\n\nThe search turned up documentation on the scopes and the token behavior, but it does not support the refresh-token and expiry assumptions in your query.\n\n- **Scopes:** The official forum post lists ACTIVITY (completed activities), WELLNESS (weight, resting HR), and CALENDAR (planned workouts), plus CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS. For each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access) and use commas to separate multiple scopes. A third-party Elixir OAuth library confirms the comma format and says the default scope is \"ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ\" (index 2-1).\n- **Token response:** The forum post shows that a successful authorization returns a Bearer token, the granted scopes, and athlete info (index 1-6). It does not mention a refresh token or `expires_in`.\n- **Refresh tokens and expiry:** The Elixir library's documentation says Tokens do not expire, and there are no refresh tokens, and that stored credentials come back with no refresh token and no expiry. This is a third-party source, so verify it against the official Intervals.icu API docs before relying on it.\n- **Scope note:** The library also says the ATHLETES scope does not work with bearer tokens, only with API keys (index 2-2).\n\nYour assumption that the flow returns `refresh_token` and `expires_in` may be wrong, so check the live token response before writing refresh logic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97975cea-5814-45b8-8cc8-614ba972b10b","uuid":"53d2a74e-dbc0-437b-b725-d3b52a402474","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:06:21.984Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu OAuth API scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR:WRITE authorize token refresh_token expires_in","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0176yVsDb8tG7F98DshSrbKi","content":[{"title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},{"title":"Überauth intervals.icu","url":"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090.md"},{"title":"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090"},{"title":"open api","url":"https://www.intervals.icu/features/open-api/"},{"title":"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io","url":"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/latest/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html"},{"title":"intervals icu tools","url":"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools"},{"title":"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io","url":"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/docs/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html"},{"title":"intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=9"}]},"The search turned up documentation on the scopes and the token behavior, but it does not support the refresh-token and expiry assumptions in your query.\n\n- **Scopes:** The official forum post lists ACTIVITY (completed activities), WELLNESS (weight, resting HR), and CALENDAR (planned workouts), plus CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS. For each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access) and use commas to separate multiple scopes. A third-party Elixir OAuth library confirms the comma format and says the default scope is \"ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ\" (index 2-1).\n- **Token response:** The forum post shows that a successful authorization returns a Bearer token, the granted scopes, and athlete info (index 1-6). It does not mention a refresh token or `expires_in`.\n- **Refresh tokens and expiry:** The Elixir library's documentation says Tokens do not expire, and there are no refresh tokens, and that stored credentials come back with no refresh token and no expiry. This is a third-party source, so verify it against the official Intervals.icu API docs before relying on it.\n- **Scope note:** The library also says the ATHLETES scope does not work with bearer tokens, only with API keys (index 2-2).\n\nYour assumption that the flow returns `refresh_token` and `expires_in` may be wrong, so check the live token response before writing refresh logic."],"durationSeconds":5.620699541000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MyYESY8QhpvEF686LhvVHQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
